07 — QR BEHAVIOR

QR SHALL resolve to a verification destination,
not to a marketing page.

QR destination must expose:

IDENTITY MATCH
STATUS
VALIDITY WINDOW
PROVENANCE POINTER
VERSION
LAST VERIFIED TIME

No silent redirects.

---

08 — STATUS MODEL

Canonical identity states:

DRAFT
PROPOSED
ACTIVE
SUSPENDED
REVOKED
ARCHIVED

Verification outcomes:

VERIFIED
UNVERIFIED
EXPIRED
UNKNOWN

No ambiguous success state is allowed.

---

09 — AUTHORITY BOUNDARY

Identity can represent:
- relation
- role
- context

Identity cannot self-grant:
- authority
- scope expansion
- constitutional exceptions

Canonical law:

IDENTITY REPRESENTS AUTHORITY CONTEXT.
IDENTITY DOES NOT GENERATE AUTHORITY.

---

10 — PROVENANCE REQUIREMENT

Each identity record should be inspectable through:

ORIGIN
ISSUER
CITADEL
WATERMERK
SEAL
PROVENANCE
VALIDITY
VERSION

If provenance is missing,
status cannot be presented as verified.

